From bd019cb2e562cd1b6ad44bc9534f0a0a03f4672f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/26] media: i2c: ov5648: keep cached control values while
 powered down

ov5648_g_volatile_ctrl() reads the exposure and gain registers over I2C
unconditionally, but the sensor is only powered between runtime resume and
suspend, so every read outside that window fails:

  'ov5648 2-0036': Unable to read control 0x00980911: No such device or address

VIDIOC_G_EXT_CTRLS then returns an error and the control is left unset.
libcamera reads the exposure while configuring, before anything has started
streaming, and its software ISP goes on to fetch the value it believes it
just read, which aborts the process:

  controls.h:189: T libcamera::ControlValue::get() const [with T = int]:
  Assertion `type_ == details::control_type<...>::value' failed.

ov5648_s_ctrl() already returns early when the device is suspended and leaves
the cached value in place; do the same when reading.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/ov5648.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5648.c b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5648.c
index 81e0e5a3277e..02bf1f419120 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5648.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5648.c
@@ -1999,6 +1999,14 @@ static int ov5648_g_volatile_ctrl(struct v4l2_ctrl *ctrl)
 	struct ov5648_ctrls *ctrls = &sensor->ctrls;
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * The registers cannot be read while the sensor is powered down, and
+	 * failing the read leaves the control unset for userspace. Keep the
+	 * cached value instead, which is what the setters already do.
+	 */
+	if (pm_runtime_suspended(sensor->dev))
+		return 0;
+
 	switch (ctrl->id) {
 	case V4L2_CID_EXPOSURE_AUTO:
 		ret = ov5648_exposure_value(sensor, &ctrls->exposure->val);
-- 
2.53.0

